#{[17592186412493 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412493 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412493 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412493 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the expression $(A∧B)∨(A∧¬B).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412493 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ce194f41-6fc2-5669-9a9a-5765a4bee419" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412493 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's simplify the expression using the properties of logical operations:\n\n- First,  we use the distributive law (conjunction over disjunction):\n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨(A∧¬B)≡A∧(B∨¬B)\n$$\n\n- Next,  we use the fact that the disjunction of an expression and its negation is a tautology:\n\n$$\nA∧(B∨¬B)≡A∧\\text{t}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we use the fact that the conjunction of an expression and a tautology gives the initial expression:\n\n$$\nA∧\\text{t}≡A\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨(A∧¬B)≡A.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412494 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412494 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412494 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412494 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412494 #edb/ref 1069 "q-218619" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412494 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412494 #edb/ref 1071 "If $P$ is a statement, $\\text{t}$ is a tautology, and $\\text{c}$ is a contradiction, complete the following table of logical equivalences.\n\n| Statement | Is Logically Equivalent To |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\text{t}∧\\text{c}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{c}∨\\text{c}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{c}∧¬P$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $P∨\\text{c}$ | {{field-4}} |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412494 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e8b03653-3dbc-58b5-96b9-61df0ae25ec2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412494 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall the following properties of tautologies and contradictions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∨\\text{t}=\\text{t}\\, &  & A∧\\text{t} & =A \\\\ A∨\\text{c}=A\\, &  & A∧\\text{c} & =\\text{c} \\\\ \\text{t}∨\\text{t}=\\text{t}\\, &  & \\text{t}∧\\text{t} & =\\text{t} \\\\ \\text{t}∨\\text{c}=\\text{t}\\, &  & \\text{t}∧\\text{c} & =\\text{c} \\\\ \\text{c}∨\\text{t}=\\text{t}\\, &  & \\text{c}∧\\text{t} & =\\text{c} \\\\ \\text{c}∨\\text{c}=\\text{c}\\, &  & \\text{c}∧\\text{c} & =\\text{c}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Statement | Is Logically Equivalent To |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\text{t}∧\\text{c}$ | $\\text{c}$ |\n| $\\text{c}∨\\text{c}$ | $\\text{c}$ |\n| $\\text{c}∧¬P$ | $\\text{c}$ |\n| $P∨\\text{c}$ | $P$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420434 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420434 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420434 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420434 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420434 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420434 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420434 #edb/ref 1045 "Tautologies and Contradictions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420434 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186420436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420434 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420434 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420434 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ca9805b2-0055-5f04-a805-328b01ff7cbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420435 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b5ec8193-89bd-513d-9413-97a3db4d604d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420435 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186412494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420436 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420436 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c3697fe6-7104-578f-a0f0-040a5a9c9a26" #e